 been prevented from delivering  crucial supplies  particularly in rural areas we are still  struggling every day to have access  to to allow our drugs and medicines and  the international  support that they they deserve to to  to get in and this is uh this is uh this  is very frustrating  this is uh something that is the most  difficult part  amnesty says it gathered testimony from  more than 40 witnesses  but the ethiopian government has  questioned the organization's findings  while the eritreans called the report  preposterous  any prospect of an international  investigation  is slim john sparks sky news
 

